# SAEA-BENCH-featcache — the owner's feature-cache vision, measured for real
# (owner directive 2026-08-11 "do not decide the scheme from observation alone; run it, measure the effect, then lock" (translated from Chinese)).
#
# Patched llama-server (local commit b3dc62149 on the pinned fdbd6abee, the
# 93-line diff archived at docs/patches/2026-08-11-mtmd-feature-cache.diff,
# bound by receipts/runtime-q4km-featcache.json): audio-chunk embeddings
# keyed by the chunk's FNV content hash, RAM layer + persistent dir carried
# in server_env (config-hashed). A hit decodes from the cached embd and
# skips the encoder; a miss encodes and back-fills; fallback is the stock
# path.
#
# Substrate: a1a-fixed-window-ojw — fixed windows make slice bytes
# run-invariant (A-1a verdict, same day: fixedwindow also WINS the WER
# contrast by 6.7 pp at 20% fewer calls), so the warm run's keys are
# byte-identical to the cold run's.
#
# Protocol: the SAME arm runs twice under one row. COLD attempt builds the
# cache (encode + back-fill); WARM attempt consumes it. Pre-registered
# readings: (i) warm wall vs cold wall — THE measured benefit the lock
# decision waits on; (ii) warm server log shows feat-cache HIT lines and
# zero "encoding mtmd batch" lines; (iii) warm WER vs cold WER — same
# config hash, fixed windows: this doubles as the CASCADE-FREE determinism
# repeat (byte-compare transcripts); (iv) cold wall vs the unpatched
# fixedwindow arm (2a0d08, 20 min) — the patch's overhead when cache is
# empty must be ~zero.
#
# run_id:baseline_fragment
SAEA-BENCH-featcache:a1a-fixed-window-ojw
